    "title": "Ten Somali Women Begin Media Internships in Mogadishu",
    "original_title": "10 Young Women Begin Journalism Internships Across Somalia",
    "slug": "ten-somali-women-begin-media-internships-in-mogadishu",
    "summary": "Ten female students from three Mogadishu universities have started a four-month journalism internship at six local media outlets, aimed at building practical skills and increasing women's representation in Somali newsrooms.",
    "content": "Ten young women enrolled at three universities in Mogadishu have commenced a four-month journalism internship programme that places them within six of Somalia's media organisations. The participants are students from Somali National University, Mogadishu University, and Hormuud University.\n\nThe interns will work across Somali National News Agency (SONNA), Radio Muqdisho, Somali National Television, Astaan Media, Radio Kulmiye, and Shabelle Radio TV during the programme. The placement is designed to give the participants direct exposure to newsroom operations, reporting, and production work while they complete their university studies.\n\nThe initiative addresses a long-standing gap in Somali media, where women remain underrepresented in editorial and technical roles despite making up a significant share of communications and journalism graduates. By pairing students with established outlets, the programme seeks to convert academic training into practical experience that can lead to employment.\n\nFor the Somali diaspora, the development is relevant on several levels. Many diaspora families support relatives studying in Mogadishu and follow Somali media closely for news from home. An expanded cohort of trained female journalists may contribute to more diverse coverage and new perspectives in outlets that diaspora audiences rely on. Diaspora professionals in media and communications have also funded or mentored similar training efforts in the past, and the programme creates a potential pipeline for collaboration between Somali newsrooms and diaspora expertise.\n\nThe internships run for four months. Neither the organisers nor the participating media houses have announced whether the programme will be repeated or expanded in future intakes.\n\nRead the original report from Radio Dalsan here: https://radiodalsan.com/2026/09/15/10-young-women-begin-journalism-internships-across-somalia/?utm_source=rss&#038;utm_medium=rss&#038;utm_campaign=10-young-women-begin-journalism-internships-across-somalia",
