    "content": "On September 15, 2026, Somalia's Acting Minister of Defense, MP Omar Ali Abdi, received a delegation from the African Union Counter-Terrorism Centre (AUCTC) in Mogadishu. The delegation was led by AUCTC Director Idriss Mounir Lallali. The meeting focused on enhancing cooperation between Somalia and the African Union in combating and preventing terrorism.\n\nThe discussions come as Somalia continues efforts to bolster its security institutions and military capabilities. The meeting underscores the importance of international partnerships in addressing the persistent threat posed by militant groups in the region.\n\nThe AUCTC, based in Algiers, provides support to African Union member states in counter-terrorism efforts, including capacity building and intelligence sharing. Somalia has been a key partner in these initiatives, given its long-standing fight against al-Shabaab and other extremist groups.\n\nFor the Somali diaspora, this meeting signals ongoing international support for Somalia's stability. Many diaspora members have family ties to affected regions and contribute to rebuilding efforts. Enhanced security cooperation can lead to improved safety and economic opportunities, both locally and for those abroad.\n\nRead the original report from Goobjoog here: https://goobjoog.com/2026/09/15/soomaaliya-oo-xoojinaysa-iskaashiga-midowga-afrika-ee-la-dagaallanka-argagixisada/",
