    "content": "Mogadishu, September 15, 2026 — Prime Minister Hamza Abdi Barre of the Federal Republic of Somalia welcomed three Somali students at his office today. The students, Abdulqani Abdulqadir Sheikh Hussein, Abdulrahman Qasim Mohamed, and Abdulrahman Ahmed Mahmoud, secured first, second, and third places respectively in an international Quran recitation competition held in Qatar.\n\nThe competition, which drew participants from various countries, highlighted the students' exceptional skill in Quranic recitation. Their success brings national pride and underscores the importance of religious education within Somalia and its diaspora. The Prime Minister's reception reflects the government's acknowledgment of their achievement.\n\nDuring the meeting, Prime Minister Barre announced that the government will provide higher education opportunities for all three students. This commitment aligns with broader efforts to support youth education and promote cultural and religious excellence. The specifics of the educational support are yet to be detailed.\n\nFor the Somali diaspora, this event resonates deeply, as many families prioritize both secular and religious education. The students' success serves as an inspiring example for young Somalis worldwide, encouraging them to pursue excellence in their studies and faith. It also strengthens ties between Somalia and Qatar, a key partner in educational and religious initiatives.\n\nThis recognition comes amid ongoing efforts by the Somali government to invest in youth as a means to foster national unity and development. The Prime Minister's gesture highlights the value placed on educational achievement and its role in shaping future leaders.\n\nRead the original report from Goobjoog here: https://goobjoog.com/2026/09/15/dowladda-soomaaliya-oo-bixinaysa-waxbarashada-tacliinta-sare-ee-saddexda-arday-ee-ku-guuleystay-tartanka-quraanka/",
